<%#
  The area's own contextual menu, on every screen of it.

  Core's own workflows/_action_menu has two links and is rendered from two of its
  four screens; this one is rendered from all four, because the summary and the
  copy screen are as much part of the area as the matrices are -- with the link
  to the screen you are already on left out.

  The diagnostics page is here rather than in Redmine's administration menu since
  WP19: ADR-003 costed one extra line in that menu and a page you visit when
  something is wrong is not worth a second (finding F07). This is where somebody
  who has just been told the host has drifted is standing.

  The last link leaves the area: Redmine's own workflow screens, which since
  ADR-003 are the generic workflow and nothing else. One of the two cross-links
  the ADR asks for; the other is on core's screen and points back here.

  Locals: current -- :summary, :copy or nil for the two matrices.
%>
<div class="contextual">
  <% unless current == :copy %>
    <%= project_workflows_icon_link('copy', l(:button_copy), copy_project_workflow_rules_path) %>
  <% end %>
  <% unless current == :summary %>
    <%= project_workflows_icon_link('summary', l(:field_summary), project_workflow_rules_path) %>
  <% end %>
  <%= project_workflows_icon_link('list', l(:label_project_workflow_inventory),
                                  project_workflow_inventories_path) %>
  <%= project_workflows_icon_link('help', l(:label_project_workflow_diagnostics),
                                  project_workflow_diagnostics_path) %>
  <%= project_workflows_icon_link('workflows', l(:label_project_workflow_generic_screens),
                                  edit_workflows_path) %>
</div>
